From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Maus <mail@jens-maus.de>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: bcm2710-rpi-2-b/3-b: reset the LAN9514 through
 LAN_RUN

The onboard LAN9514 USB hub and Ethernet controller of the Raspberry
Pi 2 Model B and 3 Model B stays powered across a warm reboot. When
the firmware does not reset it, it sometimes does not come back: no
hub, no eth0 and no USB devices until a power cycle.

Its nRESET input is driven by LAN_RUN, which is GPIO 31 on the 2 B
and line 3 of the firmware GPIO expander on the 3 B. Describe it as
the reset GPIO of the hub node, so that onboard_usb_dev pulses it
whenever the kernel boots.
---
 arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2710-rpi-2-b.dts | 7 +++++++
 arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2710-rpi-3-b.dts | 7 +++++++
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2710-rpi-2-b.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2710-rpi-2-b.dts
index ce48eb6..c0bfd0b 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2710-rpi-2-b.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2710-rpi-2-b.dts
@@ -202,3 +202,10 @@ i2c_csi_dsi0: &i2c0 {
 		pwr_led_trigger = <&led_pwr>,"linux,default-trigger";
 	};
 };
+
+&usb {
+	usb1@1 {
+		/* LAN_RUN (GPIO 31) drives the LAN9514 nRESET */
+		reset-gpios = <&gpio 31 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+	};
+};
diff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2710-rpi-3-b.dts b/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2710-rpi-3-b.dts
index 35e6e99..c018fb8 100644
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2710-rpi-3-b.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2710-rpi-3-b.dts
@@ -291,3 +291,10 @@ i2c_csi_dsi0: &i2c0 {
 		pwr_led_trigger = <&led_pwr>,"linux,default-trigger";
 	};
 };
+
+&usb {
+	usb1@1 {
+		/* LAN_RUN on the firmware GPIO expander drives the LAN9514 nRESET */
+		reset-gpios = <&expgpio 3 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+	};
+};
-- 
